# Once this became a git repo, Railway began honouring .gitignore as well — which excludes data/*.db and site/ because
# both are build products that must not be versioned. That silently shipped an image with no archive and no pages.
# Anything the running service needs is re-included here explicitly, and `npm run smoke` checks it after every deploy.
!data/record.db
!site
!site/**
data/pump.db*
# data/seed.db is NOT shipped. It was, deliberately, for the two boots that merged it (13:12 and 14:13 on
# 2026-09-08, both recorded in the collector's `seed_merges`); this is the negation being removed afterwards, which
# the plan called putting the shovel back. Leaving it in bakes 91 MB into every image for no benefit, and worse: the
# merge is keyed on the seed's size and hash, so the day someone re-runs `npm run seed` the next ordinary deploy
# would carry a file with a new key and merge it on boot, unasked. To seed a fresh collector, re-add `!data/seed.db`
# here and in .dockerignore for that one deploy, then take both out again.
data/seed.db*
data/archive.db*
data/reports
data/run.log
data/telegram.session
data/*.jsonl
site/t
site/w
# The per-token and per-wallet JSON that `npm run site --pages` writes for an offline copy. These moved from
# site/api/{t,w} to site/api/v1/{token,wallet} when the API was versioned; the old rules silently stopped matching,
# which is how a --pages run would have shipped tens of thousands of files into the image. The live routes are served
# dynamically by serve.ts and matched before the static tree, so nothing here is needed at runtime.
site/api/v1
node_modules
*.log
.env
.env.bak.*
